[quote="Anubis"]

That's a good way to do what I wanted. I just feel people are dismissing my idea based solely on lack of a quality then trying to interpret it  using  what qualities I have isn't that what the system is going for?

[/quote]

&nbsp;

You are in the right. As long as you can justify it in a cool comic book way. Thats what I grrl this is. Storytelling, and overall "that sounds awesome". It seems that your DM is trying a little to be numbers and details. WHo cares if you're not 5 feet away. Or if you're not in perfect hiding. It needs to be aethetcally ool.&nbsp;

[quote="rickjonzz"]

FTR, this is really only a problem when playing a pregen with a limited subset of the rules available. The full description of the standard Qualities (like Creativity) should explain just what Creativity covers.&nbsp;

Qualities sort of seem like Aspects from Fate and require agreement as to when it applies. I might think&nbsp;that "Private Investigator" covers punching because PIs get in lots of fights. The GM might say "no, you need a separate skill for that" and we'd hash it out during character creation.&nbsp;

[/quote]
 I agree with parts of this. If Anubis was making Unity in character creation, he'd probably want to give her ranged combat as a quality, but she's already finished and doesn't have that, and that's where the problems arise. If possible (and if it's not too late), try talking to your gm about retconning one of her qualities into ranged combat, maybe banter or creativity.

[quote="jlabrecque42"]

I would say that yes, technically Unity is a technomancer, so she has the ability to telekinetically deconstruct metal and bend it to her will. However, as a GM, I would probably steer you away from launching metal shards at things because it doesn't fit her character.&nbsp; Unity has honed her ability to have the precision to assemble highly functional robots that help her get things done.&nbsp; While she may have the psychic ability to hurl metal at things, Unity as a character would look down on such a blunt solution.&nbsp;I think her affinity for her robots makes it more likely that she would construct a scorpion bot with a large stinger that could shoot it at her enemies.&nbsp; Or even better, a porcupine!&nbsp; Not nearly as efficient, but that is who she is.&nbsp;

When I think metal + creativity, I think of constructing an earthworm bot that can fold itself into a key to unlock a door.&nbsp; Again, not as efficient, but Unity will always make a bot to do a thing&nbsp;rather than do it herself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

[/quote]
Which is largely how my players played her, too. One built a gun turret robot, and expended a boost bot and a personal boost to get a d12 minion walking cannon.
